        "position": 6,
        "title": "OK but not tick repellent",
        "text": "I bought this because Nexgard was not repellent/ preventative (and had a scary history of seizures in some dogs). My problem was mostly ticks picked up during hikes. My boy does not really hang out with other dogs for long so fleas were not an issue. Vectra does kill ticks but only after they latch on and hitch a ride home with my dog. They'll usually die and fall off in 24h. So it is not repellent as advertised.Another problem is application: it is too liquid and tends to empty all up on lower back (nothing left in the tube by the time you get to upper back/shoulders) and it leaks for a while after application and takes a long time to dry. Unlike what is advertised, it also leaves residue on the dog fur for several days.Plus the price rose by about $25.00 since I last bought a batch on Amazon last year! Dog \"owners\" are not cash cows!!",
